W95FA font

STATUS: NOT ESTABLISHED. Do not move this font to assets/fonts/ until the
paragraph below can be replaced with the licence text itself.

What is known
-------------

The font was obtained from dafont, which lists it as "SIL Open Font License"
and as free for personal and commercial use:

    https://www.dafont.com/w95fa.font

That is a third party's summary of the terms, not the terms. The SIL Open
Font License asks that its text travel with the font, and no copy of it
arrived with this download -- so what is on disk here is a font file and a
claim about it, which is not the same thing as a licence.

Why that matters here
---------------------

GlitchVape ships two typefaces under the OFL, and it does it by including the
licence file each author published beside their font, so that the about window
and `glitchvape --licenses` quote the real document rather than a paraphrase
somebody maintains in Perl. This font cannot be shipped that way yet, because
there is no document to quote.

So it is packaged in glitchvape-fonts-extra rather than in the base package,
which exists precisely so that the base package can state one honest licence
-- MIT AND OFL-1.1 AND LicenseRef-VCR-OSD-Mono -- and carry nothing whose
terms are unverified.

Note that "no licence text" is not by itself what puts a font here. VCR OSD
Mono has no licence document either, and it ships in the base package, because
its author was asked and answered: see ../../fonts/VCROSD/LICENSE. What is
missing for W95FA is not the paperwork but the answer.

What would settle it
--------------------

Either the upstream release containing OFL.txt, from the author rather than
from a font aggregator, or the author saying so where it can be cited -- which
is exactly how VCR OSD Mono stopped being a question. With that in hand, W95FA
is an ordinary bundled font and the directory moves to assets/fonts/, at which
point the Makefile ships it without anyone editing a list.
